// DISCRIMINATION CASE 1 (grep flags it -- and is right, but only flags).
//
// This is a *response*-sum spend-cap policy: the temporal sum quantifies over
// `Transfer::response` rows (settled completions only).  The current event is
// a request, never a response, so it is EXCLUDED from the sum by event kind
// (under the closed/reflexive `formerly within` window), and in-flight
// (issued, not-yet-responded) transfers are invisible to the sum.  A
// keyword/pattern scan ("response-sum => in-flight invisible => UNSAFE")
// flags this as buggy -- and is right.
//
// ROTN agrees (UNSAFE at every K) and adds what the scan cannot: a concrete
// witness whose shape tracks the concurrency bound K (the client-side
// request-pool size), and a sound proof that no other failure exists:
//
//   K = 1  ->  UNSAFE.  The parallel-fire race is unexpressible, but the
//                       sequential off-by-one is not: a fire is admitted
//                       with the settled amount already at the cap, and it
//                       settles to > cap.  Witness:
//                       {completed: 200, inflight: 1}  (200 + 100 > 200).
//   K >= 2 ->  UNSAFE.  Two or more un-settled fires can each pass the guard
//                       (settled still 0) and settle to > cap.  Witness at
//                       K=3: {completed: 0, inflight: 3}  (3 x 100 = 300 > 200).
//
// The SAME policy text and the SAME keyword at every K -- the witness shape
// is what tracks the bound the environment imposes on in-flight concurrency.
// See docs/discrimination.md.
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace (alert_total_transfer_over_200 schema).
// TransferInput carries `amount: Long`; TransferOutput is empty.

@id("discrimination_response_sum_bounded")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum a for (a: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::response{ input.amount: a } && tp(t))
    )) <= 200
};
